## Electrochemical Sensors

Sensor is a device that detects physical or chemical properties by converting chemical energy into electrical signal.

### Potentiometric Sensors

Potentiometric sensors measure the potential difference between working and reference electrode.

### Example

pH glass electrode

### Amperometric Sensors

The sensor measures flow of current between working electrode and reference electrode. Using this, redox reactions can be measured.

### Example

Glucose sensor

