## Corrosion

It is the destruction of metal by chemical reactions with the surrounding environment like gases or liquids.

---

## Types of Corrosion

### Dry Corrosion

Dry corrosion is direct chemical reaction between a metal and dry gases without presence of moisture.

### Galvanic Corrosion

It takes place when different metals are touching each other in presence of corrosive environment. The more active metal acts as anode.

### Differential Aeration Corrosion

It takes place when a metal is exposed to different air concentrations. The well aerated part acts as cathode.

### Factors Affecting Corrosion

- Purity of the metal
- Temperature
- Presence of moisture

---

## Types of Protection

### Cathodic Protection

Cathodic protection is a method used to protect metals from corrosion by making the metal surface act as a cathode.

### Anodic Protection

It is a corrosion control method in which electrical current is applied to keep metals in a passive state.

---

## Surface Coating Methods

Surface coating protects the metal by separating it from the environment.

### Galvanizing

Galvanizing is the process of coating iron or steel with a thin layer of zinc to prevent corrosion.

### Tinning

Tinning is the process of coating iron or steel with a thin layer of tin.